    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0165" n="99" xml:id="pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4607: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-14T12:00:00-05:00">January 14,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. My No. 12, January 14, 3 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">a.m.</hi>] I think it
                    is safe to say that a government headed by Mendieta and supported by Batista
                    will represent a majority of the Cuban people: both of them without question are
                    extremely popular in very different sectors of the public.</p>
                <p>I again respectfully urge immediate action in order to avert a catastrophe: the
                    only other section of the public which has any chance of reaching power at this
                    time is the extreme left.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
